[text] Planning summary — Phase 2b.3 architecture (drawn from the existing decision memo §2b.3):
- **`phone/motion.ts`** (pure): `magnitudeG`, `createImpulseDetector(thresholdG, debounceMs)`, `computeCalibrationThreshold(peaks[])`. No DOM/sensor APIs.
- **Wire-format additions**: `{ type: 'sample'; t; peakG }` (phone→laptop during calibration) and `{ type: 'config'; thresholdG; debounceMs; mode: 'armed'|'calibrating' }` (laptop→phone).
- **`engine/types.ts`**: optional `phoneCalibration?: { thresholdG; calibratedAt }` on `DrillConfig`. Optional → no Dexie schema bump.
- **`PhoneApp.tsx`**: adds an "Enable motion" button (iOS calls `requestPermission` if present), registers `devicemotion`, runs detector, sends `commit` (armed) or `sample` (calibrating) over the DataChannel.
- **`ui/CalibrateScreen.tsx`** (new): collects 5 sample peaks, computes p10−ε threshold, persists to active profile, sends `mode:'armed'` back to the phone. Mounted inside `PairScreen` when peer is connected (sharing peer via Zustand is a 2b.4 problem per the memo).
- **`docs/SETUP_IOS.md`** (new): mkcert HTTPS walkthrough.
- **`app/verify-phase-2b3.mjs`** (new): C-gate checks for the static UI; M1–M6 manual real-device checklist per §B2.
